DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/film-screening-prisoner-no-62
 6710-is-present-orqaidi-no-626710-haazir-hai\n\nThis event is co-sponsored
  by the Center for South Asia and the Department of Art and Art History.\n
 \nPrisoner No. 626710 is Present chronicles the arrest and prolonged incar
 ceration of activist Umar Khalid\, accused of orchestrating the 2020 New D
 elhi riots. Through archival footage and personal accounts\, Lalit Vachani
  explores Khalid’s activism\, the impact of his imprisonment on his part
 ner Banojyotsna Lahiri\, and the broader crackdown on dissent under the Mo
 di government. The film situates Khalid’s story within the larger politi
 cal repression of civil rights movements and Muslim voices in India.
END:VEVENT
